<title>SPAIN: Spain confirms plans to buy 87 Eurofighters.</title>
<headline>Spain confirms plans to buy 87 Eurofighters.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain confirmed on Friday that it would devote up to 25 billion pesetas next year toward the purchase of 87 Eurofighter combat aircraft, the Industry Ministry said.</p>
<p>Spain joined Britain in declaring it would help fund serial production of the fighter by a four-country consortium, starting next year.</p>
<p>The other two consortium members are Germany and Italy.</p>
<p>Spain's total multi-year investment in Eurofighter production will be nearly one trillion pesetas between 1997 and 2010, the Ministry of Defence said.</p>
<p>The investment, which is not expected to weigh on the 1997 budget, is expected to help create 22,000 jobs in Spain.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
